  "productUrl": "https://www.roche-bobois.com/en/product/sense-4-seat-sofa/A126021602.html",
  "notes": "Roche Bobois Sense (Studio Roche Bobois), the curved 4-seat sofa, 260 cm, with its deep end on the LEFT as you face it (x < 0; on the right of someone sitting on it). Sizes from Roche Bobois's technical sheet (technicals.roche-bobois.com/M125338841/TDSv_SENSE_2024.pdf, page 2, the 4-seater \"XSX\" in the plan \"ÉLÉMENT MESURE B\", the wall along its back): 260 wide and 146 deep overall, 107 deep at its shallow right-hand end (the product page's 107 cm), 75 high, seat height 38, black metal legs 6 cm high. Plan for the full 260 × 146 cm footprint; the sheet's plan \"MESURE A\" (255 × 153) is the same sofa turned. The same sofa as the 240 (sofa-roche-bobois-sense-240-left), 20 cm longer, the extra length mostly in the long straight stretch of seat and back towards the right end. Roche Bobois's photos show the other hand, with the deep end on the right as you face it; the sheet has both, and the app can't mirror an item, so this item is the deep-end-left one only. model.glb is generated by `npx tsx tools/models/sofa-roche-bobois-sense-260-left.ts` from its own geometry after the sheet's plan, traced (it draws the deep end 143.5 deep; the trace stretches the deep end alone to 146), the sheet's elevation and the photos, with the 240's shapes: one buttoned, pebble-shaped base on six black legs, and a thick buttoned roll wrapping round it as the back, leaning back, with rounded pads as its ends. The seat is three surfaces (the middle, the deep end and the right end), so cushions and throws can go on it. The fabrics are planning colours, not Roche Bobois's (the default olive is close to its photos); fabric.espresso, fabric.dark-chocolate, fabric.dark-walnut and fabric.dark-umber are dark browns to try, alongside the chocolates, also planning colours rather than Roche Bobois swatches. No clearance zone: the legroom in front of the shallow seats lies inside the item's box, beside the deep end."
